WEBVTT

1
00:00:13.100 --> 00:00:16.042
next morning I heard a knock on the door of our apartment.

2
00:00:17.423 --> 00:00:18.684
Molly stood outside.

3
00:00:20.065 --> 00:00:22.927
She was wearing her bathrobe and her walking boot.

4
00:00:24.047 --> 00:00:26.669
It was a good thing she only had to walk across the hall.

5
00:00:27.750 --> 00:00:28.590
She looked worried.

6
00:00:28.610 --> 00:00:30.231
"Iggy," she said.

7
00:00:32.060 --> 00:00:34.961
"I have a big problem and you've got to help me!"

8
00:00:36.862 --> 00:00:37.602
"What's wrong?"

9
00:00:38.123 --> 00:00:38.643
I asked.

10
00:00:39.643 --> 00:00:43.265
But then I remembered all the sounds I'd heard last night.

11
00:00:44.325 --> 00:00:46.466
First I'd heard a train whistle.

12
00:00:49.567 --> 00:00:53.409
Then I'd heard noises like loud roars and blaring horns.

13
00:00:54.790 --> 00:00:56.830
I was pretty sure I hadn't been dreaming.

14
00:00:56.850 --> 00:01:00.252
"Come to my apartment," said Molly.

15
00:01:00.896 --> 00:01:01.837
"And I'll show you!"

16
00:01:01.857 --> 00:01:05.740
"I'll be there as fast as I can," I said.

17
00:01:07.462 --> 00:01:09.604
I gobbled down the rest of my breakfast.

18
00:01:10.665 --> 00:01:11.926
My mom had gone to work.

19
00:01:13.908 --> 00:01:16.190
So I left Tate a note to tell him where I was.

20
00:01:17.431 --> 00:01:19.493
Then I hurried over to Molly's apartment.

21
00:01:20.493 --> 00:01:22.795
She was sitting on the couch with her foot on a pillow.

22
00:01:24.137 --> 00:01:27.720
Tufty was perched beside her with his head tucked under his wing.

23
00:01:28.780 --> 00:01:32.402
Caswell was holding a toy car as he watched the bird closely.

24
00:01:32.422 --> 00:01:38.105
"Tufty is sleeping," he whispered to me.

25
00:01:38.125 --> 00:01:40.927
"Of course he's sleeping!"

26
00:01:41.427 --> 00:01:42.148
said Molly.

27
00:01:42.168 --> 00:01:46.150
"He's tired from making loud noises all night!"

28
00:01:46.170 --> 00:01:49.532
"I heard him," I said with a nod.

29
00:01:49.552 --> 00:01:51.293
"He was pretty noisy."

30
00:01:51.313 --> 00:01:56.616
"We found out he doesn't just make roaring subway sounds," Molly went on.

31
00:01:57.440 --> 00:02:01.942
"He also knows how to imitate screeching buses and taxi horns!"

32
00:02:01.962 --> 00:02:04.783
"And racing cars.

33
00:02:04.983 --> 00:02:11.426
Vroom!" growled Caswell as he raced his toy car around the floor.

34
00:02:11.446 --> 00:02:15.588
"Everyone in our apartment building heard Tufty!"

35
00:02:16.028 --> 00:02:16.908
wailed Molly.

36
00:02:16.928 --> 00:02:20.750
"All the neighbors are complaining to my mom."

37
00:02:20.770 --> 00:02:23.471
"Oh, Iggy."

38
00:02:23.971 --> 00:02:25.512
Tears filled her eyes.

39
00:02:26.672 --> 00:02:29.794
"I'm worried that I won't be able to keep Tufty!"

40
00:02:30.835 --> 00:02:33.177
Mrs. O'Donnell appeared from the kitchen.

41
00:02:33.197 --> 00:02:36.219
"It's very serious," she said.

42
00:02:36.239 --> 00:02:38.780
"Dr. Stanley didn't sleep at all.

43
00:02:39.921 --> 00:02:40.301
And Mrs.

44
00:02:40.361 --> 00:02:42.023
Curry had to stuff cotton in her ears!"

45
00:02:43.343 --> 00:02:45.425
Tufty still had his head under his wing.

46
00:02:46.586 --> 00:02:48.767
He certainly wasn't losing any sleep!

47
00:02:50.228 --> 00:02:51.909
"Iggy," said Molly.

48
00:02:51.929 --> 00:02:55.652
"You have to think of an invention to keep Tufty quiet.

49
00:02:56.732 --> 00:02:58.293
I don't want to give him away.

50
00:02:58.313 --> 00:03:02.537
I need him to cheer me up so I can get better fast!"

51
00:03:02.557 --> 00:03:06.520
"I'll think really hard," I said.

52
00:03:06.540 --> 00:03:08.582
"Hurry up!"

53
00:03:09.142 --> 00:03:09.783
said Molly.

54
00:03:10.944 --> 00:03:13.426
A few minutes later, Josh and Jenny came over.

55
00:03:14.446 --> 00:03:16.548
They had heard Tufty during the night too.

56
00:03:16.568 --> 00:03:22.853
"Bunch howled every time Tufty made the train whistle noise," said Jenny.

57
00:03:22.873 --> 00:03:27.320
"And Sparky hid under the bed," said Josh.

58
00:03:28.361 --> 00:03:30.262
Sparky was Josh's hamster.

59
00:03:30.282 --> 00:03:36.164
"Iggy is going to think of a way to keep Tufty quiet," said Molly.

60
00:03:36.184 --> 00:03:39.306
"I'm sure you'll think of something, Iggy."

61
00:03:39.766 --> 00:03:40.406
said Jenny.

62
00:03:40.426 --> 00:03:44.148
"Remember when you figured out I had the wrong glasses on?"

63
00:03:44.168 --> 00:03:48.309
"And when you invented the Fabulous Glasses-Finder?"

64
00:03:48.790 --> 00:03:49.450
said Molly.

65
00:03:49.470 --> 00:03:52.531
"And don't forget my bell!"

66
00:03:53.071 --> 00:03:53.972
said Caswell.

67
00:03:55.260 --> 00:03:58.243
"It helped everyone find me whenever I got lost!"

68
00:03:59.323 --> 00:04:01.906
I was happy my friends thought I was a good inventor.

69
00:04:03.747 --> 00:04:06.649
But it was hard to think with everyone staring at me.

70
00:04:07.750 --> 00:04:10.112
Plus, Molly was telling me to hurry.

71
00:04:11.333 --> 00:04:12.434
I closed my eyes.

72
00:04:12.454 --> 00:04:19.760
"Vroom!" said Caswell, still racing his little car around the floor.

73
00:04:19.780 --> 00:04:24.364
"Maybe I'd better go into solitary confinement," I said.

74
00:04:25.728 --> 00:04:26.869
"What does that mean?"

75
00:04:27.390 --> 00:04:28.010
asked Jenny.

76
00:04:28.030 --> 00:04:33.935
"It means I have to go somewhere by myself and think," I explained.

77
00:04:35.776 --> 00:04:39.480
But before I could go into solitary confinement, something happened.

78
00:04:40.680 --> 00:04:41.821
Actually, two things happened.

79
00:04:42.882 --> 00:04:45.945
First the lights came back on in Molly's apartment.

80
00:04:46.886 --> 00:04:49.868
The workmen must have finally put in the new wires.

81
00:04:51.149 --> 00:04:54.212
The second thing that happened is that I got an idea.

82
00:04:55.177 --> 00:04:57.790
I guess my head got some new wires in it too!
